@startuml EditSequenceDiagram
title Baker edits an order: edit ORDER_ID [fields...]  (alias: update)

actor Baker
participant "BakerCli" as Cli
participant "Parser" as Parser
participant "UpdateOrderCommand" as Cmd
participant "OrderList" as List
participant "Order" as Order

Baker -> Cli : edit O001 s/10 d/22-10-2026
Cli -> Parser : parseUpdate(input)
activate Parser
note right of Parser
  At least one field is required.
  null in UpdateOrderDetails means
  "field not supplied, keep the
  old value". Supplied date/size
  are validated as in add.
end note
Parser --> Cli : UpdateOrderDetails\n(O001, size=10, dueDate=..., rest null)
deactivate Parser
Cli -> Cmd : new UpdateOrderCommand(details...)
Cli -> Cmd : execute(orders)
Cmd -> List : getById("O001")
List --> Cmd : original Order
Cmd -> Cmd : build updated Customer / Cake\nkeeping every unsupplied field
Cmd -> Order : updatedCopy(customer, cake, dueDate)
Order --> Cmd : new Order, same ID and status
Cmd -> List : update(updatedOrder)
note right of List
  update replaces the record with
  the same ID in place; the ID,
  status and list position are
  unchanged.
end note
Cmd --> Cli : Updated order O001: ...
Cli --> Baker : print confirmation
@enduml
